instruction:
Run the complete floorplan stage for the synthesized gcd netlist in one script, without modifying the netlist:
1. initialize the floorplan with a target core utilization of 30%, a core aspect ratio of 1.0 and 4 um of core-to-die spacing on all four sides, with standard-cell rows of site FreePDK45_38x28_10R_NP_162NW_34O;
2. create the routing tracks for all ten routing layers (metal1 to metal10);
3. place all IO pins on the die boundary, using metal3 for pins on the left/right edges and metal2 for pins on the top/bottom edges;
4. insert TAPCELL_X1 well-tap cells in a checkerboard with a tap distance of 15 um (taps 2 x 15 = 30 um apart within a row, adjacent rows staggered by 15 um; the first and last rows may contain both phases), a TAPCELL_X1 endcap at both ends of every row, and no other cells;
5. build the VDD/VSS power grid exactly as defined by the platform PDN configuration file platform/Nangate45.pdn.tcl, with the power and ground pins of every cell, including the tap and endcap cells, connected to VDD and VSS.
